# Sprint 13 WS19 — `vercel deploy` from the CLI scans the working
# directory itself and does not reliably honour .gitignore the same way
# git does, which caused deploys to fail with "Request body too large"
# once warehouse/data/ (local-only raw datasets, 11GB, never committed —
# see .gitignore) existed on disk. Mirrors the relevant .gitignore
# entries so local raw data never gets anywhere near a deployment.
warehouse/data/
data/
*.parquet
*.duckdb
*.duckdb.wal
*.shp
*.dbf
*.shx
*.prj
*.cpg

# Standard excludes Vercel's build system regenerates anyway.
node_modules/
.next/
coverage/
